From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:23:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep tick-time scratch state per thread or per world, not
 static

Vanilla and CraftBukkit pass a few facts down a call stack through static
fields: instaFall, the sapling's tree type, the dispenser's event flag, the
block or entity behind the next damage event, the activation boxes, and the
enchantment modifiers' running totals. With one server thread that works. The
asynchronous chunk decoration already set instaFall from its own thread, and
worlds ticking on their own threads would overwrite the rest for each other.
They move to AthenaThreadState (per thread), World.athenaActivationBounds and a
per-thread set of modifiers; entity ids come from an AtomicInteger; sounds,
effects, block actions and lightning go to the players of the world they happen
in instead of every player filtered by dimension. One thread behaves as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaThreadState.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaThreadState.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4f178f8167195f3044cb18cecaa0b8c596e168c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaThreadState.java
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+package net.minecraft.server;
+
+import org.bukkit.TreeType;
+
+/**
+ * Athena - flags vanilla and CraftBukkit kept in static fields, set by one call and read by a call
+ * further down the same stack: "populating, so sand falls at once", "the sapling that grew was a
+ * birch", "the dispenser already fired its event", "the damage about to be dealt comes from this
+ * block or entity".
+ *
+ * A static is only right while one thread does all of this. The asynchronous chunk decoration
+ * already sets instaFall from its own thread, where the server thread could read it in between, and
+ * worlds that tick on their own threads would set the others mid-tick for each other. Each thread
+ * gets its own copy instead; within one thread nothing changes.
+ */
+public final class AthenaThreadState {
+
+    private static final ThreadLocal<AthenaThreadState> CURRENT = ThreadLocal.withInitial(AthenaThreadState::new);
+
+    /** BlockFalling.instaFall: falling blocks land at once instead of becoming entities. */
+    public boolean instaFall;
+    /** BlockSapling.treeType: the tree the last grow call made, for StructureGrowEvent. */
+    public TreeType treeType;
+    /** BlockDispenser.eventFired: the dispense behaviour already fired BlockDispenseEvent. */
+    public boolean dispenserEventFired;
+    /** CraftEventFactory.blockDamage: the block the next damage event comes from. */
+    public org.bukkit.block.Block blockDamage;
+    /** CraftEventFactory.entityDamage: the entity the next damage event comes from. */
+    public Entity entityDamage;
+
+    private AthenaThreadState() {
+    }
+
+    public static AthenaThreadState get() {
+        return CURRENT.get();
+    }
+}
